  "answer_text": "The thin, lightweight Columbia PFG shirts most people are referring to are commonly known as the **Columbia PFG Bahama** shirts. Here's a quick breakdown of the most popular thin/lightweight PFG shirt styles:\n\n1. **PFG Bahama Shirt** \u2013 Featuring lightweight nylon fabric in a roomy Relaxed Fit, this fishing shirt dries fast, keeps you cool, and blocks sun. It's constructed with quick-drying material that offers UPF 50 sun protection and a breezy, lightweight feel, with mesh-lined vents on the back for extra ventilation.\n\n2. **Terminal Tackle PFG Shirt** \u2013 Made from 100% recycled polyester for lightweight comfort on the water. It's equipped with Omni-Wick\u2122 advanced evaporation and Omni-Shade\u2122 UPF 50 sun protection, drying quickly and managing moisture to keep you cool and dry.\n\n3. **Tamiami Long Sleeve PFG Shirt** \u2013 This long-sleeve fishing shirt features a casual fit and an easy snap-up design with cool moisture-wicking fabric, UPF 50 sun protection, hidden mesh-lined vents in the back, and an antimicrobial treatment that helps reduce odor.\n\nThe **Bahama** is probably the most iconic of the bunch \u2014 it's the classic thin, button-up PFG shirt you see everywhere. The PFG line, which stands for **Performance Fishing Gear**, offers anglers advanced technology along with a cool, laid-back style.",
